"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:247
msgid ""
"After you have sent your email, there may be an initial delay while the "
"moderator of the list, a person who acts as editor, reviews your email to "
"see if it is relevant to the discussion. This step is required to limit the "
"junk email that gets sent out to everyone. <_:note-1/> Once your email is "
"sent to everyone on the list, someone may answer you. They may choose to "
"answer you directly, to post a response to the list, or to do both. In the "
"hours and days after posting, you can check to see if you received email and"
" check the list archives, as is explained above, to see if someone answered "
"there."
msgstr ""
"När du har skickat e-postmeddelandet kan det dröja innan listans moderator "
"har granskat meddelandet och kontrollerat att det hör till diskussionen. "
"Kontrollen begränsar mängden skräppost som skickas till alla på listan. "
"<_:note-1/> När meddelandet har skickats till listan kan någon svara dig "
"direkt, skriva ett svar till listan eller göra både och. Under timmarna och "
"dagarna efteråt kan du kontrollera din e-post och läsa listarkivet, enligt "
"beskrivningen ovan, för att se om någon har svarat där."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:280
msgid "Internet Chat (IRC)"
msgstr "Chatt på internet (IRC)"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:282
msgid ""
"The GNOME and GIMP projects maintain a series of servers to provide a world "
"wide network enabling an Internet Relay Chat (IRC) system for discussion on "
"issues related to those projects including a discussion channel dedicated to"
" <application>Gnumeric</application>. This is a system by which people can "
"communicate directly with each other by typing lines into an IRC client "
"which are then broadcast to everyone listening in a particular channel. "
"Unfortunately this manual cannot provide a full explanation for how to "
"obtain, install and use an IRC client. There are a number of such programs "
"available, many of which provide users all the freedoms which "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> provides and instructions for these can "
"be obtained from the world wide web. More information and access to such "
"software can easily be obtained by running a search in any world wide web "
"search engine for \"IRC\" and \"client\" and the name of the operating "
"system of the machine which will run the software."
msgstr ""
"GNOME- och GIMP-projekten driver flera servrar som tillsammans bildar ett "
"världsomspännande nätverk för diskussioner via Internet Relay Chat (IRC), "
"bland annat en kanal för <application>Gnumeric</application>. Deltagarna "
"skriver meddelanden i en IRC-klient som sedan visas för alla som lyssnar på "
"kanalen. Den här handboken kan tyvärr inte förklara i detalj hur du skaffar,"
" installerar och använder en IRC-klient. Det finns flera sådana program, "
"många med samma friheter som <application>Gnumeric</application>. "
"Instruktioner finns på webben. Sök efter ”IRC”, ”client” och namnet på "
"operativsystemet i valfri sökmotor för att hitta mer information och "
"program."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:302
msgid ""
"The <application>Gnumeric</application> IRC discussion channel is named "
"<literal>#gnumeric</literal> (although the number symbol, #, may not be "
"needed) and is hosted on the series of servers called "
"<literal>GIMPnet</literal>. The best way to connect to GIMPnet is using the "
"IRC server <literal>irc.gimp.org</literal>. That hostname points to a "
"variety of different servers in the United States. If you live elsewhere, "
"after you are connected you can use the chat command "
"<literal>/links</literal> to find a server which is closer on the internet "
"to your location."
msgstr ""
"Diskussionskanalen för <application>Gnumeric</application> på IRC heter "
"<literal>#gnumeric</literal> (nummertecknet # kanske inte behövs) och finns "
"på servernätverket <literal>GIMPnet</literal>. Anslut helst via IRC-servern "
"<literal>irc.gimp.org</literal>. Värdnamnet pekar på flera servrar i USA. Om"
" du befinner dig någon annanstans kan du efter anslutningen använda "
"chattkommandot <literal>/links</literal> för att hitta en server närmare "
"dig."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:315
msgid ""
"If you decide to join the discussion, please be polite, post a question or "
"comment and be prepared to wait a little bit for someone to address you. "
"Several of the developers are permanently connected to the channel and check"
" every half hour or so to see if anyone has asked a question but are working"
" on something else in the meantime. Your question may be answered right away"
" but asking questions using the mailing list may prove to be more efficient "
"since it would not require paying attention to the IRC channel discussion, "
"even if it ultimately requires longer to obtain an answer."
msgstr ""
"Var artig om du går med i diskussionen. Ställ en fråga eller skriv en "
"kommentar och var beredd på att vänta en stund på svar. Flera utvecklare är "
"ständigt anslutna till kanalen och tittar ungefär var halvtimme efter nya "
"frågor, men arbetar med annat under tiden. Du kan få svar direkt, men det "
"kan vara effektivare att fråga på e-postlistan. Då behöver du inte följa "
"IRC-diskussionen hela tiden, även om det kan ta längre tid innan du får "
"svar."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:883
msgid "Reporting a Problem"
msgstr "Rapportera ett problem"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:4
msgid ""
"<application>Gnumeric</application> is a complex computer program and "
"therefore necessarily contains some mistakes. The "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> team is keenly interested in finding "
"these errors and correcting them. Suggestions for improvement are also "
"welcome and can be submitted in the same fashion as an error report."
msgstr ""
"<application>Gnumeric</application> är ett komplext datorprogram och "
"innehåller därför oundvikligen fel. "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>-teamet vill gärna hitta och rätta dem. "
"Du kan också skicka in förbättringsförslag på samma sätt som felrapporter."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:13
msgid ""
"<emphasis> Please, help us to fix any errors by telling us about them. "
"</emphasis>"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>Hjälp oss gärna att rätta fel genom att berätta om dem.</emphasis>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:19
msgid ""
"Reports of problems with <application>Gnumeric</application> provide the "
"project with a way of making sure that the mistake is eventually fixed. "
"Often the mistake is obvious and a fix can be made immediately to be "
"included in the very next release of <application>Gnumeric</application>. "
"Occasionally, the mistake is more complex and the problem may take a while "
"to be resolved. In these cases, the report provides a way to remind the "
"developers that the problem still exists."
msgstr ""
"Felrapporter hjälper <application>Gnumeric</application>-projektet att se "
"till att fel blir rättade. Ibland är felet uppenbart och kan rättas direkt "
"så att lösningen kommer med i nästa version av "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>. Andra fel är mer komplicerade och kan "
"ta längre tid att lösa. En rapport påminner då utvecklarna om att problemet "
"fortfarande finns."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:31
msgid ""
"Mistakes in programs are often called \"bugs\" after one of the earliest "
"errors in an old machine which was actually caused by an insect entering the"
" machine and preventing a switch from closing."
msgstr ""
"Programfel kallas ofta för ”buggar”. Namnet kommer från ett av de tidigaste "
"felen i en gammal maskin, som faktiskt orsakades av en insekt som kom in i "
"maskinen och hindrade en strömbrytare från att slutas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:39
msgid ""
"The <application>Gnumeric</application> project uses a world wide web system"
" called <application>GitLab</application> to collect reports of program "
"errors and then to track these errors until they are finally fixed. The "
"system was developed as part of the <application>Mozilla</application> web "
"browser project, which explains the origin of the strange name."
msgstr ""
"<application>Gnumeric</application>-projektet använder webbtjänsten "
"<application>GitLab</application> för att samla in felrapporter och följa "
"dem tills felen har rättats. Tjänsten utvecklades inom projektet bakom "
"webbläsaren <application>Mozilla</application>, vilket förklarar det "
"ovanliga namnet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:48
msgid ""
"The process of submitting the report of a problem or of a suggested "
"enhancement is quite simple and can be completed in just a few steps. The "
"process begins with obtaining a good understanding of the problem to be able"
" to provide a detailed statement explaining the problem exactly. Next, the "
"user must open an account with the GNOME project's "
"<application>GitLab</application> system. Finally, the user must submit the "
"statement of the problem, ideally, along with some information about the "
"computer setup being used by the person experiencing the problem."
msgstr ""
"Det är enkelt att rapportera ett problem eller föreslå en förbättring och "
"det tar bara några steg. Börja med att ta reda på så mycket som möjligt om "
"problemet så att du kan beskriva det tydligt. Skapa sedan ett konto i GNOME-"
"projektets <application>GitLab</application>. Till sist skickar du in "
"beskrivningen, gärna tillsammans med information om datorn och systemet där "
"problemet uppstod."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:61
msgid ""
"The explanation given below should be sufficient to file a report. For more "
"detailed instructions, the main page of GNOME's GitLab can be found at "
"<ulink type=\"http\" url=\"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME\"> "
"<uri>https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME</uri> </ulink> and instructions can be "
"found at <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://handbook.gnome.org/issues/reporting.html\"> "
"<uri>https://handbook.gnome.org/issues/reporting.html</uri> </ulink>."
msgstr ""
"Anvisningarna nedan bör räcka för att skicka in en rapport. Mer detaljerade "
"instruktioner finns på GNOME-projektets GitLab-startsida: <ulink "
"type=\"http\" url=\"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME\"> "
"<uri>https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME</uri> </ulink>. Instruktioner finns "
"också här: <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://handbook.gnome.org/issues/reporting.html\"> "
"<uri>https://handbook.gnome.org/issues/reporting.html</uri> </ulink>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:77
msgid "Defining the error"
msgstr "Beskriv felet"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:79
msgid ""
"The most critical step is understanding the error as well as possible. This "
"requires knowing clearly what was happening before the error occurred, what "
"specifically caused the error to occur, what the error condition is and what"
" happened as a consequence of the error."
msgstr ""
"Det viktigaste är att förstå felet så väl som möjligt. Ta reda på vad som "
"hände innan det uppstod, vad som utlöste det, hur felet yttrade sig och vad "
"som hände efteråt."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:87
msgid ""
"The most helpful situation to enable the developers to find and correct the "
"error is to come up with a sequence of steps that generate the error. If the"
" error can be repeated, it can almost always be corrected. The most helpful "
"error reports include a small recipe that can cause the error to occur."
msgstr ""
"Det bästa underlaget för utvecklarna är en följd av steg som återskapar "
"felet. Om felet går att återskapa går det nästan alltid att rätta. Bra "
"felrapporter innehåller en kort beskrivning av hur felet uppstår."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:101
msgid "Opening an account"
msgstr "Skapa ett konto"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:103
msgid ""
"The first time a user uses <application>Gitlab</application>, they must "
"create an account. This account is needed to allow users to be informed of "
"the status of the bug as it is tracked by the system from submission to "
"resolution. The only requirement for opening a "
"<application>Gitlab</application> account is the possession of a valid email"
" address through which the user can receive a password."
msgstr ""
"Första gången du använder <application>GitLab</application> behöver du skapa"
" ett konto. Med kontot kan du följa felrapportens status från att den "
"skickas in tills den är löst. Det enda som krävs för att skapa ett "
"<application>GitLab</application>-konto är en giltig e-postadress där du kan"
" ta emot ett lösenord."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:114
msgid "Creating a new account"
msgstr "Skapa ett nytt konto"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:116
msgid ""
"Users of <application>Gitlab</application> are automatically redirected to a"
" login page, unless they have previously logged into the system and accepted"
" a 'cookie' with which they identify themselves. The login page has a link "
"called \"Create a new account\" which will direct users to the account "
"creation page."
msgstr ""
"Användare av <application>GitLab</application> skickas automatiskt till en "
"inloggningssida om de inte redan är inloggade och har accepterat en kaka som"
" identifierar dem. Där finns länken ”Skapa ett nytt konto” som leder till "
"sidan för kontoskapande."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:124
msgid ""
"Alternatively, by clicking on this <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://gitlab.com/users/sign_in#register-pane\">link</ulink>, users "
"can follow a shortcut directly to the account creation page."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också klicka på den här <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://gitlab.com/users/sign_in#register-pane\">länken</ulink> för "
"att gå direkt till sidan där du skapar ett konto."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:131
msgid ""
"Creating a new account is very simple. The account creation page has two "
"fields. In the first, a valid email account must be given. The second asks "
"for a name by which the user wishes to be known. After a user fills out "
"these two fields, clicking on the button labeled \"Create Account\" will "
"cause a new account to be created and an email sent to the address given in "
"the email field. The email will contain the password used to identify this "
"user."
msgstr ""
"Det är enkelt att skapa ett konto. På registreringssidan finns två fält. "
"Ange en giltig e-postadress i det första fältet och namnet du vill använda i"
" det andra. Klicka sedan på knappen ”Skapa konto”. Ett konto skapas och ett "
"e-postmeddelande skickas till adressen du angav. Meddelandet innehåller "
"lösenordet som du använder för att logga in."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:145
msgid "Logging into the account"
msgstr "Logga in på kontot"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:147
msgid ""
"After creating an account, users can visit the bug entry <ulink "
"type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnumeric/-/issues/new\">page </ulink> "
"for <application>Gnumeric</application>. Here users are asked to login with "
"their email address and password. After logging in, "
"<application>GitLab</application> will present a page to add a bug report."
msgstr ""
"När du har skapat ett konto kan du gå till sidan <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnumeric/-/issues/new\">för "
"felrapporter </ulink> för <application>Gnumeric</application>. Logga in med "
"din e-postadress och ditt lösenord. När du har loggat in visar "
"<application>GitLab</application> sidan där du kan skapa en felrapport."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:159
msgid ""
"A user who accepts cookies from <literal>gitlab.gnome.org</literal> will "
"only have to give a password the first time they visit GNOME's "
"<application>GitLab</application>. During all future visits, GNOME will "
"recognize the cookie and thereby identify the user."
msgstr ""
"Om du accepterar kakor från <literal>gitlab.gnome.org</literal> behöver du "
"bara ange lösenordet första gången du besöker GNOME:s "
"<application>GitLab</application>. Därefter känner GNOME igen dig med hjälp "
"av kakan."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:176
msgid "Filing a report"
msgstr "Skicka in en rapport"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:179
msgid ""
"In order to file a report of a problem with "
"<application>Gnumeric</application>, a <application>GitLab</application> "
"account is necessary. Please see the previous section, <xref linkend=\"sect-"
"bugs-gitlab_account\"/>, for an explanation of how to open an account."
msgstr ""
"Du behöver ett konto på <application>GitLab</application> för att rapportera"
" problem med <application>Gnumeric</application>. Läs föregående avsnitt, "
"<xref linkend=\"sect-bugs-gitlab_account\"/>, om hur du skapar ett konto."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:189
msgid ""
"The <application>Gnumeric</application> bug entry page consists of several "
"fields many of which must be filled out to provide a useful bug report. The "
"most important of these will be the \"Bug Description\" which contains both "
"the brief \"Summary\" field which acts like an email subject line and the "
"detailed description field \"Step to reproduce the bug\" which should be "
"used to give a more complete explanation of the problem and, ideally, to "
"describe step by step how to reproduce the bug. The only other field which "
"is required is the \"Component\" field which can be set to \"General\" and "
"left to the developers to define more specifically. The remaining fields can"
" be helpful, since they provide extra information which may help resolve the"
" problem, but are not necessary. After filling out these three fields, a "
"user can, if they desire, simply skip to the bottom and press the "
"<guibutton>Commit</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""
"Sidan där du rapporterar fel i <application>Gnumeric</application> "
"innehåller flera fält. Fyll i de viktigaste för att rapporten ska bli "
"användbar. Fältet ”Beskrivning av felet” är viktigast och innehåller både "
"det korta fältet ”Sammanfattning”, som fungerar som ämnesrad i ett "
"e-postmeddelande, och det utförliga fältet ”Steg för att återskapa felet”. "
"Beskriv problemet där och ange helst steg för steg hur det kan återskapas. "
"Det enda andra obligatoriska fältet är ”Komponent”. Du kan välja ”Allmänt” "
"och låta utvecklarna precisera det senare. Övriga fält är frivilliga men kan"
" innehålla information som hjälper till att lösa problemet. När de tre "
"obligatoriska fälten är ifyllda kan du gå längst ned och klicka på "
"<guibutton>Skicka in</guibutton>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:208
msgid "Accessing the GNOME project's GitLab"
msgstr "Öppna GNOME-projektets GitLab"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:210
msgid ""
"There are several ways to file a bug report through "
"<application>GitLab</application>."
msgstr ""
"Det finns flera sätt att skicka in en felrapport via "
"<application>GitLab</application>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:215
msgid ""
"One of the entries in the <guimenu>Help</guimenu> menu is called "
"<guimenuitem>Report a Problem</guimenuitem>. This menu entry should cause a "
"browser window to launch and open <application>GitLab</application> to the "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> page."
msgstr ""
"Menyn <guimenu>Hjälp</guimenu> innehåller alternativet "
"<guimenuitem>Rapportera ett problem</guimenuitem>. Det öppnar en webbläsare "
"och går till <application>Gnumeric</application>s sida i "
"<application>GitLab</application>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:223
msgid ""
"Alternatively, users can click on this <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnumeric/-/issues/new\"> link</ulink> "
"to access the <application>Gnumeric</application> page in "
"<application>Gitlab</application>."
msgstr ""
"Du kan också klicka på den här <ulink type=\"http\" "
"url=\"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnumeric/-/issues/new\">länken</ulink> "
"för att öppna <application>Gnumeric</application>s sida i "
"<application>GitLab</application>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:230
msgid ""
"If neither of those shortcuts work, the user must use a web browser to "
"access the following location: <_:screen-1/> The simplest way would be to "
"use the mouse to copy the text and paste that text into the location bar of "
"a web browser."
msgstr ""
"Om inget av de här sätten fungerar öppnar du följande adress i en "
"webbläsare: <_:screen-1/>. Kopiera texten och klistra in den i webbläsarens "
"adressfält."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:239
msgid ""
"The user may be asked to login, by giving their account name and their "
"password, when they begin their browser session with "
"<application>GitLab</application>. See <xref linkend=\"sect-bugs-"
"gitlab_account-login\"/> for an explanation of how to login to "
"<application>GitLab</application>."
msgstr ""
"När du öppnar <application>GitLab</application> i webbläsaren kan du behöva "
"logga in med ditt kontonamn och lösenord. Läs <xref linkend=\"sect-bugs-"
"gitlab_account-login\"/> om hur du loggar in på "
"<application>GitLab</application>."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:251
msgid "The Bug Description"
msgstr "Beskrivning av felet"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:253
msgid ""
"A useful error report will include a subject that describes the error "
"concisely, has a brief introduction which explains in greater detail what "
"happened and, ideally, has a small recipe that leads to the error being "
"repeated."
msgstr ""
"En användbar felrapport har en kort ämnesrad som beskriver felet och en "
"inledning som förklarar vad som hände. Beskriv helst också hur felet kan "
"återskapas."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:260
msgid ""
"The summary field, like the subject of an email message, briefly describes "
"the problem. For example, a useful error report might have a summary "
"\"Gnumeric crashes when saving a file\"."
msgstr ""
"Sammanfattningsfältet beskriver problemet kort, ungefär som ämnesraden i ett"
" e-postmeddelande. En användbar sammanfattning kan till exempel vara "
"”Gnumeric kraschar när en fil sparas”."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:273
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" \n"
"This report describes an error which causes Gnumeric to crash\n"
"during the use of the file save dialog.\n"
"\n"
"1) Start a new Gnumeric\n"
"2) In Cell A1 type \"hello\"\n"
"3) From the \"File\" menu, select \"Save As\"\n"
"=&gt; The \"Save As dialog\" opens up\n"
"4) In the file name box, type \"my_spreadsheet.gnumeric\"\n"
"5) Click on the \"Save\" button\n"
"=&gt; I expected the file to be saved, and to be able to keep\n"
"working but instead Gnumeric disappeared and the file was \n"
"never saved.\n"
"\n"
"thanks, \n"
"a user\n"
msgstr ""
" \n"
"Rapporten beskriver ett fel som får Gnumeric att krascha\n"
"när dialogrutan för att spara filer används.\n"
"\n"
"1) Starta ett nytt Gnumeric\n"
"2) Skriv ”hej” i cell A1\n"
"3) Välj ”Spara som” på menyn ”Arkiv”\n"
"=&gt; Dialogrutan ”Spara som” öppnas\n"
"4) Skriv ”mitt_kalkylblad.gnumeric” i filnamnsfältet\n"
"5) Klicka på knappen ”Spara”\n"
"=&gt; Jag förväntade mig att filen skulle sparas så att jag kunde fortsätta\n"
"arbeta, men i stället försvann Gnumeric och filen\n"
"sparades inte.\n"
"\n"
"Tack,\n"
"en användare\n"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:267
msgid ""
"The field titled \"Steps to reproduce the bug\" should contain a slightly "
"expanded version of the summary giving an overview of the problem and then "
"give a step-by-step example of how to reproduce the problem. For example, "
"this field could look like the following: <_:screen-1/>"
msgstr ""
"Fältet ”Steg för att återskapa felet” bör innehålla en något längre "
"sammanfattning med en överblick av problemet och en stegvis beskrivning av "
"hur det kan återskapas. Fältet kan till exempel se ut så här: <_:screen-1/>"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:298
msgid "Product and Component"
msgstr "Produkt och komponent"

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:300
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Product</emphasis> should be set to "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> since the GNOME version of "
"<application>GitLab</application> is used for all the different programs in "
"the project."
msgstr ""
"Välj <emphasis>produkt</emphasis> <application>Gnumeric</application>, "
"eftersom GNOME-versionen av <application>GitLab</application> används för "
"alla program i projektet."

#. from gnome:reviewed/gnumeric/master/help
#: C/gnumeric.xml:307
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Component</emphasis> describes the part of "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> that causes the problem. This may not be"
" obvious so, unless one of the other entries clearly matches, the component "
"should be set to \"General\". The possible components for "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> are as follows."
msgstr ""
"<emphasis>Komponent</emphasis> anger vilken del av "
"<application>Gnumeric</application> som orsakar problemet. Det är inte "
"alltid uppenbart. Välj därför ”Allmänt” om ingen annan komponent passar "
"tydligt. Möjliga komponenter för <application>Gnumeric</application> listas "
"nedan."

